const encoder = new TextEncoder();

const WORKING_SET_SKILL_MD = `---
name: working-set
description: "Use selectively for session-local synthesis across uploads or live Office data when concise notes will prevent repeated source reads."
platform: officeai
---

# Working Set

Create a small, temporary working set under /home/user/uploads/working-set/ only when a multi-source task will reuse the same findings across several steps. This is an optional scratch layer, not a knowledge base, workflow tracker, authorization boundary, or source of truth.

## Ownership Boundaries

- Raw uploads and live Office content remain authoritative. Never overwrite them.
- Indexed organizational knowledge belongs to the LLMWiki MCP server. Start with its retrieve_wiki tool and preserve section_id and heading_path citations.
- Do not copy MCP passages into the working set by default. Save only derived notes that materially avoid repeated work, and retain the authoritative section ids.
- Use update_todos for workflow state. Do not create current-task.md, log.md, checklists, or another progress system here.
- Treat every working-set file as session-local and user-scoped. Never use it as durable memory or a permission decision.

## When To Use

Use this skill when all of the following are true:

- The task spans multiple uploads, sheets, messages, or document sections.
- The same extracted facts will be reused in later analysis or generation steps.
- A compact note will cost less than rereading the authoritative sources.

Skip it for simple lookups, one-pass transformations, a single small file, or any task that can proceed directly from current Office context.

## Procedure

1. Inspect the relevant sources with the native Office, read, bash, or LLMWiki MCP tools.
2. Decide whether repeated reads are actually likely. If not, continue without creating a working set.
3. Write the smallest useful artifact, normally one of:
   - /home/user/uploads/working-set/summary.md
   - /home/user/uploads/working-set/evidence.md
   - /home/user/uploads/working-set/outputs/<deliverable>.md
4. For each derived claim, retain a source path, sheet/range, message/document identifier, or LLMWiki section id.
5. Validate important claims against the authoritative source before producing the final deliverable.
6. Prune stale notes rather than accumulating a second corpus.

## Spreadsheet Coverage

For large or multi-sheet workbooks, track coverage in update_todos and process explicit sheet/range batches. The working set may hold compact findings, but it must not replace range-level read-back validation or silently omit oversized sheets.

## Anti-Patterns

- Do not mirror every upload or search result.
- Do not maintain an index and activity log for routine tasks.
- Do not cite a working-set note when the original source or MCP section id is available.
- Do not write bookkeeping files instead of completing the user's requested Office action or deliverable.
`;

